WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.750
Step 1: Open Rostering → Leave. Your annual leave card shows the tracked balance, available hours after booked leave, accrual and reserved hours. Authorised reviewers can select a staff member. Casual employees do not earn paid annual leave.

2
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:31.458
Step 2: Use Set starting balance once for existing staff. Enter the confirmed payroll hours at the start of the selected date. Normal paid hours can prefill all-day leave; keep unknown days blank and exclude breaks and overtime. Save explicitly. Earlier history is covered by this starting amount. A future starting date activates tracking when it arrives.

3
00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:51.083
Step 3: Approve timesheets to accrue one hour of annual leave for every thirteen eligible ordinary hours. Approved paid absences also accrue leave when their confirmed dates finish. On leave approval, review the ordinary paid hours, excluding public holidays from annual leave. Unconfirmed hours make the balance incomplete; Paid leave hours confirms them later. Cancelling approved leave releases its reservation.

4
00:00:51.083 --> 00:01:09.792
Step 4: Open a shift’s dollar icon → Costs for super, annual leave provision and employer estimate. Super defaults to 12% of eligible ordinary-time earnings. Under-18 staff qualify when recorded employer work exceeds thirty hours in the week. Existing explicit overrides remain available. Annual leave provision includes estimated loading; ordinary gross wages and budget calculations stay separate.
